# Official production app standards

This is a live Geocon production app. Treat every change as if hundreds of people may be using the site while you push.

## Continuous deploy safety

- Users must keep working during and after a deploy (no forced logout, no broken board mid-edit when avoidable).
- Prefer additive, backward-compatible API/UI changes. Old clients and in-flight sessions must still work until the new build is fully live.
- Do not require coordinated downtime for routine feature work.
- CI gates (tests) must pass before deploy; never ship knowingly breaking changes.

## Backward compatibility

- Do not remove or rename API fields, DB columns, env vars, or event types without a migration path and a deprecation window.
- New code must tolerate older data shapes (missing optional fields, nulls, legacy enum values).
- Client and server must not assume every row was written by the latest schema.

## Database migrations

- Every schema change ships as an idempotent migration under `lib/db/migrations/` and is applied by the deploy pipeline.
- Prefer expand → migrate → contract:
  1. Add new columns/tables (nullable or with defaults)
  2. Dual-write / backfill if needed
  3. Only later remove old columns after data is safe
- Never drop/rename columns or change types in a way that breaks the currently running app before the new code is deployed.
- Migrations must be safe to re-run (tracked + skip already-applied).

## Product quality bar

- Official app UX: clear errors, confirm destructive actions, no half-broken flows.
- Persist correctly; audit meaningful mutations when applicable.
- Prefer fixing forward with migrations over one-off manual DB edits.
